{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-svelte"},{"type":"text","value":". Import the UI factory from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook({ options, ...components })"},{"type":"text","value":" once. Your app calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppChat()"},{"type":"text","value":" to create the instance. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ui}"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{chat}"},{"type":"text","value":" into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory needs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every tool name in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". It also needs an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every interrupt id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generic.fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional. Widgets go in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", the same way Form and Table register components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server route matches the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-5.6"},{"type":"text","value":" on the OpenAI text adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./recipes/index","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chat UI recipes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n  import { createChatHook, UIChat } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui'\n  import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\n  import { z } from 'zod'\n  import Layout from './Layout.svelte'\n  import Message from './Message.svelte'\n  import Weather from './Weather.svelte'\n  import Fallback from './Fallback.svelte'\n\n  const getWeather = toolDefinition({\n    name: 'getWeather',\n    description: 'Look up weather',\n    inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n    outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n  }).client()\n\n  const chatOptions = {\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  }\n\n  const { createAppChat, ui } = createChatHook({\n    options: chatOptions,\n    components: {\n      layout: Layout,\n      message: Message,\n    },\n    partsComponents: { fallback: Fallback },\n    toolsComponents: { getWeather: Weather },\n  })\n  const chat = createAppChat()\n</script>\n\n<UIChat {ui} {chat} />","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Layout.svelte"},{"type":"text","value":" receives snippets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{@render queue()}"},{"type":"text","value":" draws pending sends. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item.cancelQueued()"},{"type":"text","value":" on a queue item to drop it. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Message.svelte"},{"type":"text","value":" receives snippet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parts"},{"type":"text","value":". A tool with an approval receives prop "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-a-component-in-its-own-file","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type a component in its own file"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$props()"},{"type":"text","value":" of a tool file with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolProps"},{"type":"text","value":". Share the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" module that you pass to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui'\n  import { chatOptions } from './chat-options'\n\n  let { part }: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'> = $props()\n</script>\n\n<strong>{part.input?.city}</strong>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Part components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>"},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part"},{"type":"text","value":" is already a text part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupt components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>"},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.payload"},{"type":"text","value":" matches the definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mapped components do not receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat"},{"type":"text","value":" as a prop. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" when a component needs live chat. That call opts the component into chat updates. Nested children can call it too."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-chat-from-ui-usechatcontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read chat from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui"},{"type":"text","value":" descriptor in a child file. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" only under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIChat"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIProvider"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { ui } from './chat-ui'\n\n  const chat = ui.useChatContext()\n</script>\n\n<p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat(chatOptions)"},{"type":"text","value":" owns the state. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the instance you passed into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIChat"},{"type":"text","value":". A call outside that tree throws."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interrupts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool approvals sit in the tool when you read the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. Put a component on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ choosePlan, fallback }"},{"type":"text","value":". An unbound interrupt uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":". Branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.kind === 'unbound'"},{"type":"text","value":" if the copy must differ."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full map is on the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"client","text":"Client","level":2},{"id":"type-a-component-in-its-own-file","text":"Type a component in its own file","level":2},{"id":"read-chat-from-ui-usechatcontext","text":"Read chat from ui.useChatContext()","level":2},{"id":"interrupts","text":"Interrupts","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-svelte`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once. Your app calls `createAppChat()` to create the instance. Pass `{ui}` and `{chat}` into `UIChat`.\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional. Widgets go in `components`, `partsComponents`, `toolsComponents`, and `interruptsComponents`, the same way Form and Table register components.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). Use `gpt-5.6` on the OpenAI text adapter.\n\nThe [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n  import { createChatHook, UIChat } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui'\n  import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\n  import { z } from 'zod'\n  import Layout from './Layout.svelte'\n  import Message from './Message.svelte'\n  import Weather from './Weather.svelte'\n  import Fallback from './Fallback.svelte'\n\n  const getWeather = toolDefinition({\n    name: 'getWeather',\n    description: 'Look up weather',\n    inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n    outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n  }).client()\n\n  const chatOptions = {\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  }\n\n  const { createAppChat, ui } = createChatHook({\n    options: chatOptions,\n    components: {\n      layout: Layout,\n      message: Message,\n    },\n    partsComponents: { fallback: Fallback },\n    toolsComponents: { getWeather: Weather },\n  })\n  const chat = createAppChat()\n</script>\n\n<UIChat {ui} {chat} />\n```\n\n`Layout.svelte` receives snippets `messages`, `interrupts`, `queue`, and `input`. `{@render queue()}` draws pending sends. Call `item.cancelQueued()` on a queue item to drop it. `Message.svelte` receives snippet `parts`. A tool with an approval receives prop `interrupt`.\n\n## Type a component in its own file\n\nType the `$props()` of a tool file with `ToolProps`. Share the same `chatOptions` module that you pass to `createChatHook`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui'\n  import { chatOptions } from './chat-options'\n\n  let { part }: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'> = $props()\n</script>\n\n<strong>{part.input?.city}</strong>\n```\n\nPart components use `PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>`. Then `part` is already a text part.\n\nInterrupt components use `InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>`. Then `interrupt.payload` matches the definition.\n\nMapped components do not receive `chat` as a prop. Call `ui.useChatContext()` when a component needs live chat. That call opts the component into chat updates. Nested children can call it too.\n\n## Read chat from `ui.useChatContext()`\n\nImport the same `ui` descriptor in a child file. Call `ui.useChatContext()` only under `UIChat` or `UIProvider`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { ui } from './chat-ui'\n\n  const chat = ui.useChatContext()\n</script>\n\n<p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n```\n\n`createChat(chatOptions)` owns the state. `ui.useChatContext()` reads the instance you passed into `UIChat`. A call outside that tree throws.\n\n## Interrupts\n\nTool approvals sit in the tool when you read the `interrupt` prop. Put a component on `interruptsComponents.tools` to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under `interruptsComponents.generic`: `{ choosePlan, fallback }`. An unbound interrupt uses `fallback`. Branch on `interrupt.kind === 'unbound'` if the copy must differ.\n\nThe full map is on the [React page](./react).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Svelte Chat UI\nid: typed-headless-ui-svelte\norder: 4\ndescription: \"Build a typed, headless Svelte 5 chat UI with createChatHook, snippets, and static components.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - createChatHook\n  - svelte\n  - headless ui\n  - ToolProps\n---\n\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-svelte`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once. Your app calls `createAppChat()` to create the instance. Pass `{ui}` and `{chat}` into `UIChat`.\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional. Widgets go in `components`, `partsComponents`, `toolsComponents`, and `interruptsComponents`, the same way Form and Table register components.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). Use `gpt-5.6` on the OpenAI text adapter.\n\nThe [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n  import { createChatHook, UIChat } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui'\n  import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\n  import { z } from 'zod'\n  import Layout from './Layout.svelte'\n  import Message from './Message.svelte'\n  import Weather from './Weather.svelte'\n  import Fallback from './Fallback.svelte'\n\n  const getWeather = toolDefinition({\n    name: 'getWeather',\n    description: 'Look up weather',\n    inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n    outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n  }).client()\n\n  const chatOptions = {\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  }\n\n  const { createAppChat, ui } = createChatHook({\n    options: chatOptions,\n    components: {\n      layout: Layout,\n      message: Message,\n    },\n    partsComponents: { fallback: Fallback },\n    toolsComponents: { getWeather: Weather },\n  })\n  const chat = createAppChat()\n</script>\n\n<UIChat {ui} {chat} />\n```\n\n`Layout.svelte` receives snippets `messages`, `interrupts`, `queue`, and `input`. `{@render queue()}` draws pending sends. Call `item.cancelQueued()` on a queue item to drop it. `Message.svelte` receives snippet `parts`. A tool with an approval receives prop `interrupt`.\n\n## Type a component in its own file\n\nType the `$props()` of a tool file with `ToolProps`. Share the same `chatOptions` module that you pass to `createChatHook`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte/ui'\n  import { chatOptions } from './chat-options'\n\n  let { part }: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'> = $props()\n</script>\n\n<strong>{part.input?.city}</strong>\n```\n\nPart components use `PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>`. Then `part` is already a text part.\n\nInterrupt components use `InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>`. Then `interrupt.payload` matches the definition.\n\nMapped components do not receive `chat` as a prop. Call `ui.useChatContext()` when a component needs live chat. That call opts the component into chat updates. Nested children can call it too.\n\n## Read chat from `ui.useChatContext()`\n\nImport the same `ui` descriptor in a child file. Call `ui.useChatContext()` only under `UIChat` or `UIProvider`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { ui } from './chat-ui'\n\n  const chat = ui.useChatContext()\n</script>\n\n<p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n```\n\n`createChat(chatOptions)` owns the state. `ui.useChatContext()` reads the instance you passed into `UIChat`. A call outside that tree throws.\n\n## Interrupts\n\nTool approvals sit in the tool when you read the `interrupt` prop. Put a component on `interruptsComponents.tools` to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under `interruptsComponents.generic`: `{ choosePlan, fallback }`. An unbound interrupt uses `fallback`. Branch on `interrupt.kind === 'unbound'` if the copy must differ.\n\nThe full map is on the [React page](./react).\n"}
